Problem Statement
geeksforgeeks.org
A celebrity is a person who: Knows no one. Is known by everyone else. Given an N × N matrix: M[i][j] = 1
→ i knows j
Find the celebrity. Return: Celebrity Index
OR
-1
if no celebrity exists. In an interview, you can explain it like this: Check every person individually. Verify whether they know nobody and everybody else knows them. This requires checking an entire row and column for every person. Time Complexity: O(N²)
Space Complexity: O(1)
Brute Force Code
